-- title:
--   p-adically complete ring with residue field mathbf Fₚ is a DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and let $p$ be a prime number. Assume that the image of $p$ in $\mathcal O$ is a non-zero-divisor, that $\mathcal O$ carries an algebra structure over which $\mathbf Z/p$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra (i.e. a ring homomorphism $\mathcal O \to \mathbf Z/p$) whose kernel is exactly the principal ideal generated by $p$, and that $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for that ideal $(p)$ in the sense of Mathlib's `IsAdicComplete`, namely both Hausdorff (the intersection of the powers $(p)^n$ is zero) and complete for the $(p)$-adic filtration. The conclusion asserts the existence of an `IsDomain` instance on $\mathcal O$ and, relative to it, an `IsDiscreteValuationRing` instance, together with the two statements that $p$ is irreducible in $\mathcal O$ and that the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$ as a local ring equals the ideal generated by $p$. Thus $\mathcal O$ is a complete discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$ and residue field $\mathbf F_p$; the instance data are produced existentially, so that they may be introduced by the caller.
--
--   This is the standard recognition criterion for $\mathbf Z_p$-like coefficient rings: a $p$-adically complete and separated ring with residue ring $\mathbf Z/p$ and $p$ a non-zero-divisor is a complete discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$. It serves as the bridge between the hypotheses under which coefficient rings appear in the deformation-theoretic and Honda-system parts of the development and the discrete valuation ring structure required there; several statements on $p$-divisible groups, Honda systems and deformation base change invoke it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsAdicComplete_exists_isDomain_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_ker_algebraMap_zmod_eq_span.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u

theorem IsAdicComplete.exists_isDomain_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_ker_algebraMap_zmod_eq_span
    {𝓞 : Type u} [CommRing 𝓞] (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (hp : (p : 𝓞) ∈ nonZeroDivisors 𝓞)
    [Algebra 𝓞 (ZMod p)] (hker : RingHom.ker (algebraMap 𝓞 (ZMod p)) = Ideal.span {(p : 𝓞)})
    [IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {(p : 𝓞)}) 𝓞] :
    ∃ (_ : IsDomain 𝓞) (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝓞),
      Irreducible (p : 𝓞) ∧ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝓞 = Ideal.span {(p : 𝓞)} := by sorry
